# Git commits

Only commit when the user asks. Use Conventional Commits.

```
<type>[optional scope]: <short description>
```

## Types for this repo

- `test`: new or updated specs / page objects
- `fix`: flaky test, locator, or CI failure
- `ci`: GitHub Actions / Playwright config used by CI
- `chore`: deps, gitignore, non-user-facing cleanup
- `docs`: README or comment-only docs
- `refactor`: same behavior, clearer structure

## Style

- Imperative, lowercase description, no trailing period: `test(login): cover invalid password`
- Scope is optional: `login`, `ci`, `pages`.
- Body only when the why is not obvious.
- Do not mention Cursor, co-authors, or tools unless the user asked.

```text
test(checkout): assert out-of-stock error

The cart API returns 400 when item 3 is unavailable.
The spec now covers that failure path.
```
